# Component styles

One root class per component. Store it in script and reuse it in the template and SCSS. Do not repeat the class string in the template.

```ts
const rootClass = 'miraicms-admin-header'
```

```vue
<div :class="rootClass">
  <div :class="`${rootClass}__main`">
```

Elements are `` `${rootClass}__name` ``. A hyphen continues that element: `__settings-nav` belongs to `__settings`, and `__grid-file-icon` belongs to `__grid` then `__grid-file`. Modifiers use `--` (`__item--active`).

Each attribute appears once on an element. A class plus a state object share one `:class`. A second `:class`, `:style`, or any other repeated attribute is a compile error.

```vue
<div :class="[`${rootClass}__step`, { 'is-active': active }]">
```

Scoped SCSS uses the same name. Nest under `#{$root}`: hyphen parts with `&-`, modifiers with `&--`, states with `&.` and `&:`. Do not leave `__settings-nav` as a sibling of `__settings`.

```scss
@use "../../assets/styles" as *;

$root: '.miraicms-admin-header';

#{$root} {
  display: flex;

  &__main {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  &__settings {
    display: grid;

    &-nav {
      display: flex;
    }

    &-item {
      width: 100%;

      &.is-active {
        color: $color-accent;
      }
    }
  }

  &__grid {
    &-file {
      &-icon {
        display: flex;
      }
    }
  }
}
```

In the form and SEO packages, import tokens with `@use "miraicms-nuxt/styles" as *;`. Use `$color-*`, `$shadow-*`, and `math-rem()` from that import.

`@include miraicms-wrapper` wraps rules in `body#miraicms-body` so host CSS does not override the shell. Use it for admin pages and shell chrome: pages, menu, header, user menu, entry forms, notices. Put `#{$root}` inside the mixin. Leave fields, parts, and controls (buttons, selects) unwrapped. Follow the nearest component of the same kind.
